Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not use duloxetine if you are allergic to duloxetine.
Do not take duloxetine within 5 days before you have used an MAO inhibitor.
Do not take duloxetine within 14 days after you have used an MAO inhibitor.
Examples of MAO inhibitors include isocarboxazid, linezolid, methylene blue injection, phenelzine, and tranylcypromine.
A dangerous drug interaction could occur.
Tell your doctor if you also use stimulant medicine, opioid medicine, herbal products, or medicine for depression, mental illness, Parkinson's disease, migraine headaches, serious infections, or prevention of nausea and vomiting.
An interaction with duloxetine could cause a serious condition called serotonin syndrome.
Duloxetine is not approved for use by anyone younger than 7 years old.
To make sure duloxetine is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have:
heart problems, high blood pressure;
liver or kidney disease;
slow digestion;
a seizure;
bleeding problems;
sexual problems;
narrow-angle glaucoma;
bipolar disorder (manic depression);
drug addiction or suicidal thoughts;
Triplet: ["duloxetine", "contraindicated with", "MAO inhibitor within 14 days after use"]

The relation 'contraindicated with' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug should not be used in combination with or near the time of use of the substance or medication specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'contraindicated in': The subject drug should not be used by patients who have the condition or characteristic specified by the object entity.
B. 'should be avoided with': Patients taking the subject drug should avoid the substance or activity specified by the object entity.
C. 'should not be used in place of': The subject entity should not be substituted for the object entity in treatment.
D. 'may be used for': The subject drug may be used for the purpose or condition specified by the object entity.
E. 'not approved for': The subject drug is not approved or not recommended for use in the patient population specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
